<%# One account and the pools that live inside it. See the UI design spec §4.3.
    Locals: `presenter` (HomePresenter), `account` (a Pool of type account).

    The header carries the account's buffer — `current_buffer_for`, the cash sitting there
    right now, NOT the presenter's #projected_buffer, which is a period-wide figure the
    standing band already states. A target on an account is the buffer marker (a health
    line, never a cap), so it is only shown when the user set one. %>
<% buffer = presenter.current_buffer_for(account) %>
<section class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded" data-pool-group="<%= account.name %>">
  <div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
    <%# Not the `uppercase` eyebrow the brief drafted and this codebase gives short labels
        like "Current Balance": an account name is a proper noun the user typed, and
        rendering "Ally Savings" as ALLY SAVINGS shouts a name back at them. Same weight as
        the attention band's heading, since both are the title of a band. %>
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900"><%= account.name %></h3>
    <%# An overdraft is the loudest thing in the app and this is the row that owns the
        number, so it says so here too rather than leaving the standing band's sentence as
        the only place a negative buffer is visible. %>
    <%# "now", and "target" rather than "of". The standing band prints a buffer too — the
        period-wide figure left AFTER this period's funding — so without the two time words
        one screen said "buffer" of two different quantities and left the reader to guess.
        And "of $2,000.00" reads as a denominator without saying what it measures: a target
        on an account is the buffer marker the user set, a health line and never a cap, so
        the label has to say the word. %>
    <span class="text-sm <%= buffer.negative? ? "text-status-danger font-medium" : "text-gray-700" %>">
      buffer now <strong><%= number_to_currency(buffer) %></strong>
      <% if account.target_amount.present? %>
        <span class="<%= buffer.negative? ? "text-status-danger" : "text-gray-400" %>">
          · target <%= number_to_currency(account.target_amount) %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </span>
  </div>

  <% pools = presenter.pools_for(account) %>
  <% pools.each do |pool| %>
    <%= render "pool_row", pool: pool, presenter: presenter %>
  <% end %>

  <%# Said plainly rather than left as an empty card: an account with no envelopes is a
      setup state, and a blank panel reads as something that failed to load. %>
  <% if pools.empty? %>
    <p class="px-6 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500">No pools in this account yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</section>
